From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:42:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mythic: exact guest RIP from host PC + AVX exoneration note
 (ml538-ml549)

BTCpu64IosRipFromHostPC / ios_fex_rip_from_hostpc: expose FEX's existing
host-PC -> guest-RIP block table to the unix side, so the Mach fault probes
can name the exact faulting instruction instead of the enclosing block
(CpuStateFrame+0x18 only syncs at block boundaries, which is why ml548
disassembled call setup instead of the store it was hunting). Zero runtime
cost -- the table already exists; returns 0 outside the block so callers can
tell "no answer" from a real RIP.

Config.json.in records the ml538 result: AVX is EXONERATED for the render
corruption. disableavx left the corruption identical while the writer census
changed completely, which exonerates the vector blitter paths generally, not
just AVX. Reverted rather than kept -- an unproven change does not ship.

Also: iOS JIT alias mapping export, TSO handler config, WinAPI IO cleanups.

